From dbae318eae296d07078039ecc3879935b35b0afd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sysretq0 <324514544+sysretq0@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 03:47:43 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] net: wwan: Add MediaTek MT6789 CCCI/CCIF0 modem core driver

Add clean mainline driver for the MediaTek MT6789 (Helio G99 / Gen95)
integrated cellular modem (Phase 5.2):
- Verifies LK md1img pre-load via ccci_tag_mem without touching
  EMI-MPU-protected md1img DRAM from the AP CPU.
- Executes the EL3 SiP SMC boot handshake (MTK_SIP_KERNEL_CCCI_CONTROL:
  MD_CHECK_DONE, MD_FLIGHT_MODE_SET, MD_KERNEL_BOOT_UP), SPM SRCLKEN O1
  configuration, vmodem/vsram 825 mV regulators, and MD MTCMOS cycle.
- Initializes Gen95 CCIF0 normal/exception ringbuffers in AP-MD SMEM,
  handles CCIF0 data0/data1 and MD WDT interrupts, and performs the
  HS1/HS2 runtime feature negotiation.

Signed-off-by: sysretq0 <324514544+sysretq0@users.noreply.github.com>
